{"base_rate":0.4052631578947368,"brier":0.14330894736842106,"bss":0.4054185725778646,"bss_hi":0.48937281719791614,"bss_lo":0.32192596039849136,"chart":{"base":[412.3,134.0],"fp":[294.3,249.3],"lead":"62,259.5 272,248.3 482,229.2 692,210.3","note":{"base":"skill 0.41 — higher than 76% of cities","fp":"low end +5pp, high end +12pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 64% of cities","rel":"promised 2% → rained 7%; promised 100% → rained 83%"},"rel":"76,434.4 283.3,332.6 559.8,157.4 689.9,106"},"country":"AU","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.07836842105263161,"ess":244.1621763013351,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Brisbane</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Brisbane rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>83%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>4%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 760 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nBRISBANE, 1.8 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.41, ranked 52 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(24&ndash;90) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>4%</b></td><td class='num'>227</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>8%</td><td class='num'><b>19%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>24%</td><td class='num'><b>21%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>47%</td><td class='num'><b>41%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>70%</td><td class='num'><b>70%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>88%</td><td class='num'><b>73%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>83%</b></td><td class='num'>156</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Brisbane</b> <span class=\"muted\">Australia</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;41% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 41% of days.</p><p>The forecast did clearly better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.41</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>24&ndash;90\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>760 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Brisbane &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Brisbane\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.247577092511015,377.1894273127753 86.08081081081082,327.8918918918919 143.47236842105264,257.4736842105263 222.7797260273973,172.57534246575344 304.5587012987013,88.90909090909088 370.85324675324676,36.909090909090935 410.82000000000005,18.0 410.82000000000005,22.66666666666663 370.85324675324676,88.90909090909088 304.5587012987013,164.54545454545456 222.7797260273973,252.35616438356166 143.47236842105264,324.5263157894737 86.08081081081082,372.1621621621622 59.247577092511015,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"234.4842105263158\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"234.4842105263158\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.247577092511015,369.17180616740086 86.08081081081082,313.1351351351351 143.47236842105264,305.36842105263156 222.7797260273973,232.4109589041096 304.5587012987013,126.72727272727272 370.85324675324676,117.27272727272725 410.82000000000005,78.66666666666663\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 4% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 227 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.247577092511015\" cy=\"369.17180616740086\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 8%&amp;#10;It rained 19% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"86.08081081081082\" cy=\"313.1351351351351\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 24%&amp;#10;It rained 21% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"143.47236842105264\" cy=\"305.36842105263156\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 47%&amp;#10;It rained 41% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"222.7797260273973\" cy=\"232.4109589041096\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 70%&amp;#10;It rained 70% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"304.5587012987013\" cy=\"126.72727272727272\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 88%&amp;#10;It rained 73% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"370.85324675324676\" cy=\"117.27272727272725\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 83% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 156 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.82000000000005\" cy=\"78.66666666666663\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(41%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Brisbane the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.51) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.22).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>24%</td><td class='num'>0.223</td><td class='num'>8.7%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>174</td><td class='num'>45%</td><td class='num'>0.277</td><td class='num'>10.0%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>220</td><td class='num'>52%</td><td class='num'>0.440</td><td class='num'>6.3%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>182</td><td class='num'>38%</td><td class='num'>0.514</td><td class='num'>6.5%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":-27.46794,"lon":153.02809,"n":760,"n_cities":216,"name":"Brisbane","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.003524229074889868,"n":227,"obs":0.03524229074889868,"sig":true},{"hi":0.14,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.07932432432432432,"n":74,"obs":0.1891891891891892,"sig":true},{"hi":0.37,"lo":0.14,"mean":0.2414473684210526,"n":76,"obs":0.21052631578947367,"sig":false},{"hi":0.61,"lo":0.37,"mean":0.4654794520547946,"n":73,"obs":0.410958904109589,"sig":false},{"hi":0.8,"lo":0.61,"mean":0.6964935064935064,"n":77,"obs":0.7012987012987013,"sig":false},{"hi":0.96,"lo":0.8,"mean":0.8837662337662338,"n":77,"obs":0.7272727272727273,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.96,"mean":0.9966666666666668,"n":156,"obs":0.8333333333333334,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":1.8,"provisional":false,"rank":52,"rank_hi":90.0,"rank_lo":24.0,"reliability":0.009816428498116259,"resolution":0.10623349796015273,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"brisbane","station":"BRISBANE